<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan overnight rates crash on surplus funds.</title>
<headline>Pakistan overnight rates crash on surplus funds.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Overnight rates in the Pakistani money market crashed to close at 3.00 percent on Saturday owing to excess liquidity after opening at 15 percent, dealers said.</p>
<p>The prevalent liquidity compelled borrowers to lower their bids, a dealer at KASB &amp; Co said.</p>
<p>The market closed around 3.00 percent and some banks were left with some surplus funds, he said.</p>
<p>-- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
